<title>NETHERLANDS: Schiphol air cargo up 2.9pct in January.</title>
<headline>Schiphol air cargo up 2.9pct in January.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Schiphol airport saw total freight handled in January rise to 85,000 tonnes, a increase of 2.9 percent over the same month last year.</p>
<p>In a statement, the airport said the growth was smaller than might have been expected due to less freight than usual being carried on scheduled flights.</p>
<p>It added that aircraft movements stood at 26,300 in January, a gain of 9.4 percent, with growth reported on short-haul European feeder routes.</p>
<p>				 Jan 1996   97 vs 96</p>
<p> Air transport movements  26,300	 up  9.4pct</p>
<p> Passengers(x 1,000)	 1,924	 up 10.2</p>
<p> Freight (Tonnes)	   85,000	 up  2.9</p>
